<title>USA: St. Paul unit takes stake in WebTV.</title>
<headline>St. Paul unit takes stake in WebTV.</headline>
<dateline>BLOOMINGTON, Minn. 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>St. Paul Venture Capital, a unit of St. Paul Cos, said Monday it has taken a stake in privately held  WebTV Networks Inc of San Francisco.</p>
<p>The size was not disclosed. St. Paul Venture Capital typically makes $1 million to $10 million investments in emerging U.S. growth companies.</p>
<p>WebTV Networks has developed set-top boxes that link a consumer's television and phone lines with the Internet.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
